# ADR-000: Bootstrap

## Status

Accepted on bootstrap.

## Context

`{{ project_name }}` was created from the `library-java` Copier template at `ika100/sdlc-foundry`. The template encodes the platform's Java library conventions (platform ADR-009 for the tooling, ADR-125 for publishing):

- JDK {{ java_version }} LTS and Maven via devbox; a plain Java library, no Spring Boot
- Spotless (google-java-format) + a minimal Checkstyle config as the quality gate; trivy or OWASP Dependency-Check and detect-secrets for security
- JUnit 5, JaCoCo with an 80% line gate
- The Maven artifact `{{ group_id }}:{{ project_name }}` (jar + sources jar), deployed to GitHub Packages by the `publish` CI job of a `v*` tag; the tag is the version
- No server, no container image, no Kubernetes
- Claude Code agents from the `sdlc-foundry` marketplace (`svc-java` + `svc` + `shared`)

## Decision

We adopt the platform conventions verbatim. Any deviation must be justified in a new ADR.

## Consequences

Skeleton updates (CI, devbox recipes, the publish script, JDK bump) arrive through `copier update`; `pom.xml`, `src/`, `config/` and `docs/adr/` are project-owned and never overwritten.
